// (rule 10 allows them in a file); 3Q26 from the 8-K Ex. 99.1 earnings release of Oct 29 2026, its debt from the Form 10-Q (Oct 30 2026).
// Generated by scratchpad amzn_va/build_amzn_hm.py + emit_hm.py; not typed (3Q26 typed from the release).
//   EPS (ex-non-op) operating income × (1 − the quarter's effective tax rate) ÷ diluted shares — GAAP EPS without
//                  non-operating income (expense) (SAB, Oct 29 2026: the P/E is drawn on this basis only, because Amazon's
//                  GAAP EPS carries large marks on its Anthropic and Rivian stakes). Tax rate = income tax ÷ (net income +
//                  income tax). ⚠ 4Q22: pre-tax income was close to zero after the Rivian mark-down, so the quarter's rate
//                  is 129% and its EPS ex-non-op comes out negative (−$0.079); kept as the rule gives it, not smoothed.
//   EBITDA (adj.)  operating income + depreciation & amortization (the cash-flow line "Depreciation and amortization of
//                  property and equipment and capitalized content costs, operating lease assets, and other") + stock-based
//                  compensation — Bloomberg's IS_COMPARABLE_EBITDA basis and the Summit model's. FY2025 = $165,198M
//                  (79,975 + 65,756 + 19,467) = the four quarters below. Q4 flows = full year − nine months.
//   shares         weighted diluted shares for the quarter (millions); Q4 = the 10-K's three-month figure where it was
//                  tagged, else the full-year figure (4Q21–4Q25). Counts filed before the 20-for-1 split of June 2022 are
//                  multiplied by 20.
//   cash           cash and cash equivalents + marketable securities, period end.
//   debt           long-term debt, current + non-current, period end. 3Q26: $173,125M non-current (8-K) + $6,827M current
//                  portion (Form 10-Q 3Q26, Note 5; filed Oct 30 2026, the day after the 8-K the chart steps on).
//   net debt       debt − cash (negative = net cash). Leases are excluded, as for Alphabet.
// The "filed" date is when the 10-Q / 10-K (3Q26: the 8-K) became public; the chart steps each series on that date.
// [quarter, period end, filed, EPS ex-non-op, EBITDA adj., operating income, shares, cash, debt, net debt] — US$ million (EPS in $)
